Here's a simple user interface design with the components you mentioned:

1. Text Box:
   - The text box is a rectangular input field that allows users to enter their text. It typically has a placeholder text such as "Type your message" or "Enter your name" to guide the user's input.
   - The text box is usually located at the top of the page, below the button, and can be aligned either to the left or right of the button based on the design.

2. Button:
   - The button is a button-shaped input element that is typically designed with a rectangular shape and a contrasting color to make it stand out from the text box. It is usually labeled with a descriptive text, such as "Submit" or "Click to Send".
   - The button is typically placed below the text box, either to the left or right of the text box, depending on the design.

Here's a possible design for the user interface:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <style>
        .text-box {
            width: 200px;
            height: 40px;
            padding: 10px;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            border-radius: 5px;
            font-size: 16px;
            line-height: 24px;
            text-align: left;
        }

        .button {
            width: 100%;
            height: 40px;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 5px;
            font-size: 16px;
            line-height: 24px;
            text-align: center;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        .button:hover {
            background-color: #3e8e41;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="text-box">
        <input type="text" id="input-text" placeholder="Type your message" />
    </div>
    <button class="button">Submit</button>
</body>
</html>
```

In this design, the `text-box` element is placed below the `button` element, with a `width` of 200px and a `height` of 40px. The `padding` and `border` properties are used to create a border around the text box,

